        "text": "Level and momentum are broadly flat-to-up across the May observations, while the 2025 late-year decline indicates one-off administrative or reporting volatility. The upward May progression and downward late-2025 observation offset, so current evidence produces no material net movement from the 6.88 million prior."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: the seasonal-persistence prior is 6.88 million, with no material net update after balancing the May progression against late-2025 volatility. The complete fetched sample used for dispersion is May 2023 6.696739, May 2024 6.763710, Oct 2024 6.907747, Nov 2024 6.829321, Dec 2024 6.784735, May 2025 6.894610, Oct 2025 6.909050, and Nov 2025 6.752138 million. The seven successive changes are +0.066971, +0.144037, -0.078426, -0.044586, +0.109875, +0.014440, and -0.156912 million; sample sigma = 0.108 million, so 1.28*sigma = 0.138 million. The ladder-implied 80% bounds are 6.764 to 7.000 million, a roughly 0.118 million half-width, or about 0.85 times the dispersion benchmark; this narrower interval reflects May-seasonal anchoring and the bounded recent participation regime. The forecast horizon is about one month to the scheduled first print, not 15 months."
